mod lexical_reject_unclosed_mlstring;

// A multi-line string literal whose closing quote never comes. Its opening
// quote ends its line, so no annotation can follow it there; the one for the
// literal sits on the next line, inside what would be its content. The
// literal runs to the end of the file and the diagnostic is at the opening
// quote, on its own line, not at the line the file ends on.
//
// As in lexical_reject_unclosed_string, the missing ';' at the end of the file
// is a follow-on, and the literal is a global so that it is the only one.
// Nothing after the opening quote may hold a double quote, or it would close
// the literal: that is why the annotations carry no quoted message.

imm verse = "
  //~^ ErrorBadTok:13
  first line
  second line
//~ ErrorNoSemi follow-on
